":"ENSG00000104760","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.502835,"donor_log2fc":-0.75991,"donor_lfcse":0.416692,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00877775,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"FGL1","gene_symbol_current":"FGL1","gene_id":"ENSG00000104760","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.617674,"donor_log2fc":1.30225,"donor_lfcse":0.379124,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":1.0174,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000104760","entrez_id":["2267"],"uniprot":["Q08830"],"ncbi_summary":"Fibrinogen-like 1 is a member of the fibrinogen family. This protein is homologous to the carboxy terminus of the fibrinogen beta- and gamma- subunits which contains the four conserved cysteines of fibrinogens and fibrinogen related proteins. However, this protein lacks the platelet-binding site, cross-linking region and a thrombin-sensitive site which are necessary for fibrin clot formation. This protein may play a role in the development of hepatocellular carcinomas. Four alternatively spliced transcript variants encoding the same protein exist for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q08830","text":"Immune suppressive molecule that inhibits antigen-specific T-cell activation by acting as a ligand of LAG3 (PubMed:30580966, PubMed:35761082, PubMed:40101708). LAG3-binding initiates a signaling that inhibits the T-cell receptor (TCR) in the immunological synapse, preventing T-cell activation (PubMed:30580966). Binds LAG3 independently from MHC class II (MHC-II) (PubMed:30580966, PubMed:35761082). Secreted by, and promotes growth of, hepatocytes (PubMed:11470158, PubMed:19880967)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}